{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKzV2VqX6y15ma2hLH3n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #194 as **done** and sent it only to `triage:engineer`, with `engineer` as the worker. The result is in `.ard/194/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **What the issue asks for:** when every requested review has passed at the PR's current head, the controller should mark the worker's draft PR ready for review. It should also check open draft worker PRs on each tick, in case a mark was missed before a restart. Separately, the proposal's worker and reviewer sections contradict each other on this, and the issue asks to fix that and update the Gate 2 runbook.\n- **Why only the engineer:** it's the only triage role besides `lead` in this repository. There's no architect, product-manager or documentation-planner role to add.\n- **Protected paths:** the change doesn't touch any. It covers the reviewer loop, the effects layer, tests and docs.\n- **Reviewers:** I added no `review:` entries. `eng-review` is the only reviewer and has no `when:` rule in `.ard/config.yaml`, so it runs on every PR anyway.\n\nThe \"Open issues\" section tells maintainers two things. First, the proposal wording changes without a product or documentation planner checking it. Second, the change affects the human merge workflow, because PRs will stop being drafts once reviews pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":675,"cache_read_input_tokens":11203,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":675},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0943c08f-e53a-41b6-a3e2-bd6d1c2b6778","uuid":"777da9da-789a-4224-b35f-0ef703fdbb31","timestamp":"2026-11-23T14:08:5